atom: A1_32_credential_save_wiring
shipped_at: 2026-06-12T15:50:00Z
git_head: d3f9b659 (pre-ship)
gate: bash scripts/shipgate.sh p1

note: Pre-computer-use gap patch — two real integration seams found by code
reading after A1_31 (the kind real-test discipline exists to catch):
(1) CredentialFieldView's SecureField had NO save action — an entered key went
nowhere. Now: onSubmit + 存入 Keychain button → CredentialSubmitHandler
(injected saver; production = KeychainStore.shared.save(service: scope,
account: "api_key")). On success the field binding is CLEARED (secret never
lingers in view state); saved-confirmation line shows scope only.
(2) Scope seam: UI default scope was meta_ai_api_key while the gateway reads
deepseek-api. Now MetaAIConfigStore.load() defaults to
MetaAIConfig.deepSeekDefault() (user-ruled: openaiCompatible +
DeepSeekPresets.endpoint + DeepSeekPresets.credentialScope + v4 Pro display
name). Previously persisted configs untouched.

Architect-direct implementation (small patch, no fan-out). 8 CredentialSaveTests:
scope==presets byte-identical, account=="api_key" matches presets doc, saver
receives exact triple, whitespace trimmed, empty secret/scope short-circuit
WITHOUT calling saver, saver error surfaces without secret, load() fallback.
253 tests total (was 245), MIN_TESTS raised.
